      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Chronic headache is often a crippling condition for those afflicted by it. The case of a headache sufferer is presented here against a framework that reviews the literature on the psychological, social, and familial issues related to the problem of chronic pain. The intent is to offer practitioners guidelines and a context within which clients with chronic headache can be understood and helped."},
